' Lab 2 · Task 2 · SchemaPostol Use Case Diagram
' Actors and use cases are consistent with lab2/spec.md and lab1/model/er-diagram.mmd.
' Legend:
'   <<include>> - mandatory base use cases composing a full use case
'   <<extend>>  - optional capabilities performed together with the base use case
'   Log In (UC-02) is a PRECONDITION of the authenticated use cases (lab2/spec.md, rule 2)
'     and is therefore intentionally NOT connected via <<include>>.
'   The Author role is an elevation of the Registered User role via Microsoft OAuth
'     (lab2/adr/0005-oauth-for-authoring.md, REQ-EVN-004).
'   Litematica Parser Service is an external system actor (<<System>>), not a person.

@startuml
top to bottom direction
title SchemaPostol — Use Case Diagram (Lab 2, Task 2)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam usecaseFontSize 13
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam wrapWidth 240

' ---------- Actors (human actors declared first so they stay grouped) ----------
actor "Guest" as Guest
actor "Registered User" as RegUser
actor "Author" as Author
' External service rendered as a system component, not a person
actor "Litematica Parser Service" <<System>> as Parser

' Inheritance: Author IS-A Registered User (per lab2/spec.md)
RegUser <|-- Author

' ---------- System boundary ----------
rectangle "SchemaPostol" {

  ' --- Guest (public) use cases ---
  usecase "Register Account" as UC01
  usecase "Log In" as UC02
  usecase "Search Schematics" as UC03
  usecase "Apply Filters\n(Category, Tag, Version)" as UC04
  usecase "View Schematic Details\n(incl. Comments)" as UC05
  usecase "Download World Archive\n(optional, world_zip_url)" as UC14

  ' --- Registered User (authenticated player) use cases ---
  usecase "Write Comment" as UC06
  usecase "Save Schematic" as UC07
  usecase "Manage Profile" as UC08

  ' --- Author (Microsoft OAuth elevated) use cases ---
  usecase "Publish Schematic" as UC09
  usecase "Classify Schematic\n(Category, Tag, Version)" as UC10
  usecase "Attach World Archive\n(optional, world_zip_url)" as UC13
  usecase "Edit Own Publication" as UC12
  usecase "Delete Own Publication" as UC15

  ' --- External system use case ---
  usecase "Parse Litematica File\n(integrity + metadata)" as UC11
}

' ---------- Associations ----------
' Guest: public read-only flows
Guest --> UC01
Guest --> UC02
Guest --> UC03
Guest --> UC05

' Registered User: authenticated player flows
' (Log In is a precondition of these use cases, not an <<include>>)
RegUser --> UC06
RegUser --> UC07
RegUser --> UC08

' Author: publication flows (Author inherits from Registered User)
Author --> UC09
Author --> UC12

' External system
Parser --> UC11

' ---------- Include relationships (mandatory) ----------
UC03 ..> UC04 : <<include>>
UC09 ..> UC10 : <<include>>
UC09 ..> UC11 : <<include>>

' ---------- Extend relationships (optional) ----------
UC13 ..> UC09 : <<extend>>
UC14 ..> UC05 : <<extend>>
UC15 ..> UC12 : <<extend>>

' ---------- Notes ----------
note as N1
  **Precondition — authenticated session.**
  Log In (UC-02) is a precondition of UC-06, UC-07, UC-08
  (Registered User) and of UC-09, UC-10, UC-12, UC-13, UC-15
  (Author); it is intentionally NOT an <<include>>.
  The Author role is an elevation of the Registered User role
  via Microsoft OAuth after linking a licensed game account
  (ADR-0005 / REQ-EVN-004).
end note
RegUser .. N1

note bottom of UC11
  Background external system: validates the integrity of
  `.litematica` files and extracts metadata (dimensions,
  block counts) that flows back into the Schematic entity.
  Awaiting validation => Schematic is hidden (REQ-STA-001).
end note

note as N13
  Optional. Without a world archive
  Schematic.world_zip_url stays empty (REQ-OPT-001).
end note
UC13 .. N13

note bottom of UC12
  Only schematics where Schematic.author_id equals the
  authenticated User.user_id may be edited (REQ-UNW-002).
end note

@enduml
